WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:02.401
-The protests sweeping
the country

00:00:02.401 --> 00:00:03.836
have rocked
Donald Trump's presidency

00:00:03.836 --> 00:00:06.105
and galvanized public opinion
in favor of a fundamental

00:00:06.105 --> 00:00:08.941
rethinking of how policing works
in this country.

00:00:08.941 --> 00:00:11.244
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:11.244 --> 00:00:15.047
♪♪

00:00:15.047 --> 00:00:17.817
As we've said before, there is
probably no worse person

00:00:17.817 --> 00:00:20.086
on the face of the earth
to occupy the presidency

00:00:20.086 --> 00:00:22.154
in this moment of national
crisis than Donald Trump.

00:00:22.154 --> 00:00:24.123
We're in the middle
of a pandemic with a president

00:00:24.123 --> 00:00:27.060
who doesn't understand
or care to understand science.

00:00:27.060 --> 00:00:30.629
We're having an intense national
discussion on systemic racism,

00:00:30.629 --> 00:00:33.632
and we elected a virulent racist
and serial golfer.

00:00:33.632 --> 00:00:35.602
He's less ready to meet
the moment

00:00:35.602 --> 00:00:37.770
than the dads on "Teen Mom."

00:00:37.770 --> 00:00:39.305
Those guys are real duds.

00:00:39.305 --> 00:00:41.774
He's a soulless business potato
whose brain has been zapped

00:00:41.774 --> 00:00:43.943
by decades
of right-wing cable news

00:00:43.943 --> 00:00:45.645
and the asbestos
in his buildings.

00:00:45.645 --> 00:00:48.714
"Hold on one second, I'm gonna
take a bump of this wall candy."

00:00:48.714 --> 00:00:50.049
[ Sniffs ]

00:00:50.049 --> 00:00:52.418
Trump has always been
historically unpopular.

00:00:52.418 --> 00:00:54.320
But now,
amid nationwide protests

00:00:54.320 --> 00:00:55.721
against racist police brutality,

00:00:55.721 --> 00:00:58.524
a deadly pandemic that
he utterly failed to contain,

00:00:58.524 --> 00:01:00.927
and massive unemployment,
more Americans are coming around

00:01:00.927 --> 00:01:04.630
to the idea that maybe,
just maybe, electing a racist,

00:01:04.630 --> 00:01:07.000
Diet Coke-stained bean bag chair
wasn't the best idea.

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:08.368
Trump has sagged

00:01:08.368 --> 00:01:10.903
considerably in polls
over the last few weeks.

00:01:10.903 --> 00:01:13.406
To put it in photos,
he was here.

00:01:13.406 --> 00:01:14.807
And now he's here.

00:01:14.807 --> 00:01:18.311
Several polls have his approval
rating dipping below 40,

00:01:18.311 --> 00:01:21.781
and tied with Joe Biden
in some very unlikely places.

00:01:21.781 --> 00:01:26.485
-The new CNN national poll
shows Biden with a 14-point lead

00:01:26.485 --> 00:01:28.020
over President Trump.

00:01:28.020 --> 00:01:30.223
Our poll also shows
an overwhelming majority

00:01:30.223 --> 00:01:32.358
of Americans support
the peaceful protests

00:01:32.358 --> 00:01:33.626
and disapprove

00:01:33.626 --> 00:01:35.995
of the president's response
to the unrest.

00:01:35.995 --> 00:01:37.697
-The president's approval
rating slipped

00:01:37.697 --> 00:01:41.801
seven points in the last month,
according to a new CNN poll.

00:01:41.801 --> 00:01:44.170
And 63% of adults disapprove

00:01:44.170 --> 00:01:47.139
of how he's handled
race relations in the country.

00:01:47.139 --> 00:01:50.176
65% say his response
to the protest

00:01:50.176 --> 00:01:52.678
has done more harm than good.

00:01:52.678 --> 00:01:56.015
-The polls suggest Donald Trump
would be absolutely crushed

00:01:56.015 --> 00:01:59.719
by Joseph Biden
if the election were held today.

00:01:59.719 --> 00:02:01.620
Get this. In just the past week,
polls have come out

00:02:01.620 --> 00:02:04.991
showing Biden up by 15 points
in Michigan, up 9 in Wisconsin,

00:02:04.991 --> 00:02:09.262
up 4 in Arizona, up 2 in Ohio,
tied in Iowa, tied in Texas.

00:02:09.262 --> 00:02:12.765
-And when a Democrat is ahead in
the polls against Donald Trump,

00:02:12.765 --> 00:02:15.335
it's all over, baby!

00:02:20.506 --> 00:02:22.308
And, who knows, Texas is
historically red,

00:02:22.308 --> 00:02:23.676
but maybe Biden
has a chance there.

00:02:23.676 --> 00:02:25.511
Sure, Skateboard Jones
didn't have

00:02:25.511 --> 00:02:26.913
the best presidential campaign,

00:02:26.913 --> 00:02:28.815
but he did come within two
and a half percentage points

00:02:28.815 --> 00:02:30.850
of beating this were-badger.

00:02:30.850 --> 00:02:32.418
The "Washington Post" poll
also found

00:02:32.418 --> 00:02:34.553
that much of the opposition
to Trump is vehement,

00:02:34.553 --> 00:02:38.257
as 47% of Americans say
they strongly disapprove

00:02:38.257 --> 00:02:40.259
of the way the president
has responded to protests.

00:02:40.259 --> 00:02:43.763
Wow, it's bad enough when
the majority disapprove of you,

00:02:43.763 --> 00:02:46.799
but to have nearly half say
they strongly disapprove of you

00:02:46.799 --> 00:02:48.267
must be depressing.

00:02:48.267 --> 00:02:50.036
It's one thing if you pass
a note to a classmate that says,

00:02:50.036 --> 00:02:51.404
"Do you like me?",
and they check "No."

00:02:51.404 --> 00:02:53.772
It's another if they write in,

00:02:53.772 --> 00:02:55.775
"I'd rather eat a burrito
filled with dog turds."

00:02:55.775 --> 00:02:58.544
The polling is so bad for
Trump -- and this is true --

00:02:58.544 --> 00:03:02.048
his campaign is running ads
on TV in Washington, D.C.

00:03:02.048 --> 00:03:04.583
just so Trump
will see those ads

00:03:04.583 --> 00:03:06.519
and feel better about himself.

00:03:06.519 --> 00:03:08.354
"With their boss growing
increasingly agitated

00:03:08.354 --> 00:03:10.256
with the state
of his re-election campaign,

00:03:10.256 --> 00:03:11.691
and with the effort
of Republican critics

00:03:11.691 --> 00:03:12.925
to undermine it,

00:03:12.925 --> 00:03:14.660
President Trump's team
hatched a plan.

00:03:14.660 --> 00:03:16.195
They'd run a series
of hard-hitting ads

00:03:16.195 --> 00:03:18.498
and place them on networks
that they knew the president

00:03:18.498 --> 00:03:20.566
and Congressional Republicans
would watch.

00:03:20.566 --> 00:03:22.935
And so, over the past month,
the Trump campaign

00:03:22.935 --> 00:03:25.004
has spent
slightly more than $400,000

00:03:25.004 --> 00:03:28.040
on cable news ads
in the Washington, D.C. area,

00:03:28.040 --> 00:03:30.275
buying time largely
on Fox News

00:03:30.275 --> 00:03:34.380
but with some smaller buys
on CNN and MSNBC as well."

00:03:34.380 --> 00:03:37.983
They spent nearly half a million
dollars on ads in a city

00:03:37.983 --> 00:03:39.986
they know they won't win just so
the president will see them

00:03:39.986 --> 00:03:41.354
and feel better about himself.

00:03:41.354 --> 00:03:43.255
I mean, I guess --
I guess I get it.

00:03:43.255 --> 00:03:45.958
Sometimes I leave the
Weather Channel on for my dog

00:03:45.958 --> 00:03:48.260
so she doesn't get nervous
and chew up the sofa.

00:03:48.260 --> 00:03:49.595
Just not sure if I'd do it

00:03:49.595 --> 00:03:51.331
if it cost
half a million dollars.

00:03:51.331 --> 00:03:53.299
Seriously, at this point,
I'd say they should just

00:03:53.299 --> 00:03:54.734
sit him down
in front of "Sesame Street,"

00:03:54.734 --> 00:03:57.136
but even Big Bird would take one
look at him and say,

00:03:57.136 --> 00:03:59.171
"Hey, kid, maybe spelling's
not for you.

00:03:59.171 --> 00:04:02.608
You want to try and find a stick
while the rest of us talk?

00:04:02.608 --> 00:04:04.643
Yeah, go find a stick.
We're going to go do vowels.

00:04:04.643 --> 00:04:06.211
You go find a stick."

00:04:06.211 --> 00:04:09.114
So, Trump has seen his political
standing erode considerably.

00:04:09.114 --> 00:04:11.951
And it's especially striking
to contrast Trump's numbers

00:04:11.951 --> 00:04:15.020
with the overwhelming
public approval of the protests

00:04:15.020 --> 00:04:17.323
spurred by the horrific murder
of George Floyd

00:04:17.323 --> 00:04:18.557
at the hands of police.

00:04:18.557 --> 00:04:21.394
Majorities of Americans
are finally coming around

00:04:21.394 --> 00:04:23.395
to the reality that acts
of police violence

00:04:23.395 --> 00:04:24.830
against black people

00:04:24.830 --> 00:04:27.200
aren't just isolated incidents
from a few bad apples.

00:04:27.200 --> 00:04:29.769
They're part of a
fundamentally corrupt system

00:04:29.769 --> 00:04:33.038
based on a history of racism
and exploitation.

00:04:33.038 --> 00:04:35.474
And that is a massive shift
in public opinion,

00:04:35.474 --> 00:04:37.310
galvanized by
the nationwide protests.

00:04:37.310 --> 00:04:39.746
And not only is public opinion
changing,

00:04:39.746 --> 00:04:41.914
but so are the responses
from lawmakers.

00:04:41.914 --> 00:04:44.183
In New York, for example,
activists have sought for years

00:04:44.183 --> 00:04:46.652
to repeal a highly-restrictive
policy secrecy law

00:04:46.652 --> 00:04:48.754
known as 50-A,

00:04:48.754 --> 00:04:51.023
which shields police brutality
records from public view.

00:04:51.023 --> 00:04:53.459
But yesterday,
thanks to the protests,

00:04:53.459 --> 00:04:55.428
New York lawmakers repealed it.

00:04:55.428 --> 00:04:58.664
"The law, known as 50-A,
exceeds virtually all in America

00:04:58.664 --> 00:05:00.332
in the way
it blocks public requests

00:05:00.332 --> 00:05:02.769
for more information
on problematic officers.

00:05:02.769 --> 00:05:05.237
The controversial statute
technically keeps

00:05:05.237 --> 00:05:07.105
the 'personnel records'
of police officers,

00:05:07.105 --> 00:05:09.909
firefighters, and corrections
officers confidential

00:05:09.909 --> 00:05:12.044
and not subject
to inspection or review."

00:05:12.044 --> 00:05:14.246
I feel like they just
threw firefighters in there

00:05:14.246 --> 00:05:15.448
to make it look better.

00:05:15.448 --> 00:05:17.016
"Dave, I hear you squirted
your water

00:05:17.016 --> 00:05:18.317
next to the fire
instead of onto it.

00:05:18.317 --> 00:05:19.818
That's going in your file,
Dave."

00:05:19.818 --> 00:05:21.353
This proves once again
that direct,

00:05:21.353 --> 00:05:23.422
mass action in the streets
gets results.

00:05:23.422 --> 00:05:24.557
The demonstrations are working.

00:05:24.557 --> 00:05:26.559
Lawmakers are responding
to the pressure.

00:05:26.559 --> 00:05:27.860
Even Republicans in Congress

00:05:27.860 --> 00:05:30.262
are reportedly considering
a police reform bill.

00:05:30.262 --> 00:05:33.399
It's a sign of just how far
the politics have shifted

00:05:33.399 --> 00:05:35.167
that they're even talking
about it at all.

00:05:35.167 --> 00:05:36.702
Senate Republicans spend
most of their time

00:05:36.702 --> 00:05:39.272
rushing through unqualified
right-wing judges,

00:05:39.272 --> 00:05:41.607
conducting absurd
investigations of Democrats,

00:05:41.607 --> 00:05:44.743
and coming up with dumber
and dumber excuses

00:05:44.743 --> 00:05:46.445
for why they're not commenting

00:05:46.445 --> 00:05:48.480
on the new terrible thing
Trump has said.

00:05:48.480 --> 00:05:50.349
"Oh, yeah, no, I'm sorry,
I didn't see it.

00:05:50.349 --> 00:05:53.385
My wife, uh --
forgot to pay our Twitter bill?

00:05:53.385 --> 00:05:54.787
Is that a thing?"

00:05:54.787 --> 00:05:57.623
So, the politics of this issue
have shifted massively,

00:05:57.623 --> 00:05:59.692
thanks to protesters
and organizers

00:05:59.692 --> 00:06:01.494
in the streets,
doing the work.

00:06:01.494 --> 00:06:03.428
People across the country
have also been shocked

00:06:03.428 --> 00:06:05.464
and appalled by the countless
videos of police violence

00:06:05.464 --> 00:06:08.200
against peaceful protesters
that have circulated online.

00:06:08.200 --> 00:06:09.969
And there's a point at which
you have to ask yourself,

00:06:09.969 --> 00:06:11.137
"Can this even be reformed?"

00:06:11.137 --> 00:06:13.005
One bad flight
and you might be, like,

00:06:13.005 --> 00:06:14.440
"Maybe we can make
air travel better."

00:06:14.440 --> 00:06:16.976
But if every flight you take
ends up in the Hudson River,

00:06:16.976 --> 00:06:19.912
you might think "It's time
to de-fund Spirit Airlines."

00:06:19.912 --> 00:06:22.881
We've seen police officers
armed like they're going to war,

00:06:22.881 --> 00:06:25.751
showing up in riot gear,
beating protesters,

00:06:25.751 --> 00:06:28.186
shoving them to the ground,
hitting them with batons,

00:06:28.186 --> 00:06:29.388
trapping them on bridges,

00:06:29.388 --> 00:06:31.323
lobbing flash bangs
and pepper balls

00:06:31.323 --> 00:06:32.791
and raining down tear gas

00:06:32.791 --> 00:06:34.360
like they just turned
on the fog machine

00:06:34.360 --> 00:06:36.428
at a 12-year-old's
roller rink party.

00:06:36.428 --> 00:06:38.363
"Hey, guys, grab your skates
and get on the floor!

00:06:38.363 --> 00:06:40.333
It's Adam's bar mitzvah!"

00:06:40.333 --> 00:06:43.302
Bam-bam-ba-bam-ba!

00:06:43.302 --> 00:06:46.138
I think that was maybe a mistake
to try to make that noise.

00:06:46.138 --> 00:06:47.406
You know, if we were
in the studio,

00:06:47.406 --> 00:06:48.640
that would be a sound effect.

00:06:48.640 --> 00:06:50.009
But there you go.
That's how it went.

00:06:50.009 --> 00:06:51.543
People are increasingly
asking themselves,

00:06:51.543 --> 00:06:52.945
"Why are our tax dollars paying

00:06:52.945 --> 00:06:54.547
for these egregious
abuses of power?"

00:06:54.547 --> 00:06:57.483
Which is why you're increasingly
hearing a call from activists

00:06:57.483 --> 00:06:59.852
to dismantle police departments
and de-fund the police,

00:06:59.852 --> 00:07:02.187
a refrain that
has conservatives,

00:07:02.187 --> 00:07:04.322
and many Democrats,
freaking out.

00:07:04.322 --> 00:07:06.658
-The president tweeted
just a short time ago, quote,

00:07:06.658 --> 00:07:09.461
"Law and order, not de-fund
and abolish the police.

00:07:09.461 --> 00:07:12.498
The Radical Left Democrats
have gone crazy!"

00:07:12.498 --> 00:07:15.434
-Dangerous offspring of
this movement is --

00:07:15.434 --> 00:07:17.202
are you ready for this?

00:07:17.202 --> 00:07:18.870
De-fund the police.

00:07:18.870 --> 00:07:22.574
-This is a dangerous idea,
and it's an insane idea.

00:07:22.574 --> 00:07:26.211
-Funding of police
is a local matter, as you know.

00:07:26.211 --> 00:07:28.314
From the standpoint
of our legislation,

00:07:28.314 --> 00:07:29.982
we're not going to that place.

00:07:29.982 --> 00:07:32.184
-I don't support de-funding
the police.

00:07:32.184 --> 00:07:35.320
-In the future, the left
envisions the only people

00:07:35.320 --> 00:07:38.390
who will have guns
are people on their team.

00:07:38.390 --> 00:07:42.094
And that's exactly what de-fund
the police really means.

00:07:42.094 --> 00:07:44.597
It means a woke militia
policing our cities

00:07:44.597 --> 00:07:46.999
enforcing Democratic Party
orthodoxy.

00:07:46.999 --> 00:07:50.436
-Imagine what it's all going to
look like with no police at all.

00:07:50.436 --> 00:07:53.171
De-fund the police?
You have no police department.

00:07:53.171 --> 00:07:55.474
What are you going to do
to protect yourself

00:07:55.474 --> 00:07:57.342
and your families?
-I don't know, Sean.

00:07:57.342 --> 00:08:01.046
I just assumed you'd use
your sick MMA moves.

00:08:01.046 --> 00:08:03.782
You guys know
Jean-Claude Van Ham.

00:08:03.782 --> 00:08:06.218
Usually, MMA dudes look like
menacing fighting machines.

00:08:06.218 --> 00:08:07.620
Hannity looks like
an out-of-shape dad

00:08:07.620 --> 00:08:08.787
trying to impress his stepson.

00:08:08.787 --> 00:08:10.155
"Tyler, come on out
to the garage,

00:08:10.155 --> 00:08:11.457
I'm about to do
a roundhouse kick!

00:08:11.457 --> 00:08:13.759
Oh! My groin, Tyler.

00:08:13.759 --> 00:08:15.127
Buh!

00:08:15.127 --> 00:08:16.696
Ooh, pulled it off the bone.

00:08:16.696 --> 00:08:19.932
Get me an ice pack,
or just call the hospital."

00:08:19.932 --> 00:08:22.435
Also, Tucker, you think the left
wants to replace

00:08:22.435 --> 00:08:24.102
the police
with a "woke militia"?

00:08:24.102 --> 00:08:25.838
In your warped mind,
what do you even imagine

00:08:25.838 --> 00:08:27.806
this "woke militia"
would look like?

00:08:27.806 --> 00:08:30.376
Antifa skate teens
patrolling the streets

00:08:30.376 --> 00:08:31.510
in their "Hamilton" t-shirts,

00:08:31.510 --> 00:08:33.012
forgiving everyone's
student loans

00:08:33.012 --> 00:08:35.147
and forcing them to use their
free government healthcare?

00:08:35.147 --> 00:08:37.383
"I'm sorry, sir, I have
no choice but to detain you

00:08:37.383 --> 00:08:39.018
and bring you to the hospital
to get your rash

00:08:39.018 --> 00:08:40.486
checked out, free of charge."

00:08:40.486 --> 00:08:42.487
And then, jump on the back
of my board.

00:08:42.487 --> 00:08:45.057
And then there's Trump,
who's clearly grasping

00:08:45.057 --> 00:08:48.294
for just anything to revive
his sinking poll numbers,

00:08:48.294 --> 00:08:50.463
and who seems to be road-testing

00:08:50.463 --> 00:08:52.631
a bunch of different
attack lines all at once,

00:08:52.631 --> 00:08:55.902
mainly by changing one word
and repeating himself.

00:08:55.902 --> 00:08:57.470
-We won't be de-funding
our police.

00:08:57.470 --> 00:09:00.372
We won't be dismantling
our police.

00:09:00.372 --> 00:09:02.241
We won't be disbanding
our police.

00:09:02.241 --> 00:09:04.576
We won't be ending
our police force.

00:09:04.576 --> 00:09:07.846
-Ooh, someone got a thesaurus!

00:09:07.846 --> 00:09:09.982
I guess Trump's had a lot
of free time in that bunker.

00:09:09.982 --> 00:09:12.484
"Mr. President,
what are you doing down there?"

00:09:12.484 --> 00:09:15.320
[ As Trump ] "I am...

00:09:15.320 --> 00:09:17.723
defecating...

00:09:17.723 --> 00:09:19.725
my dungarees."

00:09:19.725 --> 00:09:21.593
And by the way, if you're
a Democratic politician

00:09:21.593 --> 00:09:23.295
who finds the phrase
"de-fund the police"

00:09:23.295 --> 00:09:25.497
somehow
politically inconvenient,

00:09:25.497 --> 00:09:28.500
because it wasn't focus-grouped
into oblivion first

00:09:28.500 --> 00:09:30.969
to ensure that it's as anodyne
and shaved-down

00:09:30.969 --> 00:09:32.137
as possible, too bad.

00:09:32.137 --> 00:09:33.539
It's not the job of activists

00:09:33.539 --> 00:09:35.407
to make you feel
comfortable politically.

00:09:35.407 --> 00:09:38.177
As Congresswoman
Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez put it,

00:09:38.177 --> 00:09:40.545
"Poll-tested slogans
and electoral feasibility

00:09:40.545 --> 00:09:42.014
is not the activists' job.

00:09:42.014 --> 00:09:43.548
Their job is to organize support

00:09:43.548 --> 00:09:45.918
and transform public opinion,
which they are doing.

00:09:45.918 --> 00:09:48.854
Our job as policymakers is
to take the public's mandate,

00:09:48.854 --> 00:09:50.922
and find and create pockets

00:09:50.922 --> 00:09:53.192
to advance as much progress
as possible.

00:09:53.192 --> 00:09:55.227
Progress takes a team
of different roles.

00:09:55.227 --> 00:09:58.063
You don't criticize a pitcher
for not being a catcher."

00:09:58.063 --> 00:09:59.331
Exactly!

00:09:59.331 --> 00:10:01.967
You criticize a pitcher
for not pitching well.

00:10:01.967 --> 00:10:03.436
Or, in the case of 50 Cent,

00:10:03.436 --> 00:10:05.337
you criticize them for agreeing
to throw out a first pitch

00:10:05.337 --> 00:10:07.539
without ever having thrown,
touched, seen, read,

00:10:07.539 --> 00:10:10.709
or even heard about baseball
before in their entire life.

00:10:10.709 --> 00:10:13.445
-And his first pitch
was not great.

00:10:13.445 --> 00:10:15.247
Just a bit outside.

00:10:15.247 --> 00:10:17.717
-We wanted to watch it again.

00:10:17.717 --> 00:10:20.552
Just let us watch it again.

00:10:20.552 --> 00:10:23.121
Instead of obsessively telling
activists and organizers

00:10:23.121 --> 00:10:24.723
in the street
doing the work

00:10:24.723 --> 00:10:26.225
how they can rewrite
their slogans

00:10:26.225 --> 00:10:27.959
to make you feel
more safer politically,

00:10:27.959 --> 00:10:30.196
maybe you can just listen
to them

00:10:30.196 --> 00:10:31.763
when they explain
what they're calling for,

00:10:31.763 --> 00:10:34.767
as Black Lives Matter
co-founder, Patrisse Cullors,

00:10:34.767 --> 00:10:36.701
did on this show last week.

00:10:36.701 --> 00:10:39.638
-If anybody has time,

00:10:39.638 --> 00:10:41.239
they should look up
their city budget.

00:10:41.239 --> 00:10:44.844
What we start to realize so much
in our communities

00:10:44.844 --> 00:10:46.812
that are divested from,
that have little access

00:10:46.812 --> 00:10:49.882
to health care,
educational opportunities,

00:10:49.882 --> 00:10:52.084
access to jobs and healthy food,

00:10:52.084 --> 00:10:55.420
is that our city governments
are using our tax dollars

00:10:55.420 --> 00:10:58.790
to primarily pay
for an economy of punishment

00:10:58.790 --> 00:11:00.759
over an economy of care.

00:11:00.759 --> 00:11:03.895
And that's what so many
Black Lives Matter organizers

00:11:03.895 --> 00:11:05.531
and organizers
that are allies

00:11:05.531 --> 00:11:07.800
of Black Lives Matter
are asking for --

00:11:07.800 --> 00:11:12.070
is to allow for a reallocation
of investment

00:11:12.070 --> 00:11:14.473
into some of
the most marginalized

00:11:14.473 --> 00:11:16.308
and divested-from
communities.

00:11:16.308 --> 00:11:17.643
-Yes!
She's right.

00:11:17.643 --> 00:11:19.278
For one thing, if you've ever
had the time

00:11:19.278 --> 00:11:20.946
to look up your city's budget,
it's now.

00:11:20.946 --> 00:11:22.815
You're probably
still in lockdown.

00:11:22.815 --> 00:11:24.250
What else are you going to do?

00:11:24.250 --> 00:11:25.884
Watch "The Sopranos" in your
sweatpants for the fourth time

00:11:25.884 --> 00:11:28.354
while you bake your eighth loaf
of banana bread?

00:11:28.354 --> 00:11:31.357
"Mmm, it's still --
still too dry."

00:11:31.357 --> 00:11:32.991
Second, an economy of punishment

00:11:32.991 --> 00:11:34.392
is the right way
to think about it.

00:11:34.392 --> 00:11:36.495
For marginalized communities
and the black community

00:11:36.495 --> 00:11:38.163
in particular,
we divest from the things

00:11:38.163 --> 00:11:40.932
that help create a healthy,
safe, equitable society,

00:11:40.932 --> 00:11:43.168
like housing and health care,
and we put that money

00:11:43.168 --> 00:11:45.404
into surveillance
and punishment instead.

00:11:45.404 --> 00:11:46.972
Just look at
the warped priorities

00:11:46.972 --> 00:11:48.474
of New York City's budget.

00:11:48.474 --> 00:11:50.175
"New York City spends more
on policing

00:11:50.175 --> 00:11:53.178
than it does on the Departments
of Health, Homeless Services,

00:11:53.178 --> 00:11:55.513
Housing Preservation
and Development,

00:11:55.513 --> 00:11:57.749
and Youth and Community
Development combined."

00:11:57.749 --> 00:11:59.385
Instead of spending all
that money on tanks

00:11:59.385 --> 00:12:01.186
and riot gear
and pepper spray for police

00:12:01.186 --> 00:12:02.387
so they can steal
people's bikes,

00:12:02.387 --> 00:12:04.023
or arrest essential
delivery workers,

00:12:04.023 --> 00:12:06.992
or slash people's tires,
or violently break up barbecues,

00:12:06.992 --> 00:12:09.695
maybe we can shift that money
to any number of other areas

00:12:09.695 --> 00:12:11.096
that actually help build

00:12:11.096 --> 00:12:12.864
safe, healthy,
equitable communities --

00:12:12.864 --> 00:12:15.568
like health care, housing,
mental health services,

00:12:15.568 --> 00:12:17.669
or, hell, just pay people
to stand in Times Square

00:12:17.669 --> 00:12:19.571
and tell tourists
where the M&amp;Ms Store is

00:12:19.571 --> 00:12:20.873
so the rest of us
don't have to.

00:12:20.873 --> 00:12:23.308
You can't reform something
while continuing

00:12:23.308 --> 00:12:25.611
to give it billions of dollars
to enact violence

00:12:25.611 --> 00:12:27.479
on marginalized communities
with impunity.

00:12:27.479 --> 00:12:29.615
Reforms are a good place
to start,

00:12:29.615 --> 00:12:32.818
but our conception
of what policing is for,

00:12:32.818 --> 00:12:34.186
and how much
policing we need,

00:12:34.186 --> 00:12:37.456
is itself something we need
to fundamentally rethink,

00:12:37.456 --> 00:12:39.958
which is why we're talking
about de-funding the police.

00:12:39.958 --> 00:12:42.528
That doesn't mean murder
will suddenly become legal

00:12:42.528 --> 00:12:44.930
and everyone will have
to take ninjutsu classes

00:12:44.930 --> 00:12:46.665
from Cobra Hair Dye over here.

00:12:46.665 --> 00:12:48.033
It just means taking money away

00:12:48.033 --> 00:12:50.102
from a fundamentally
oppressive system,

00:12:50.102 --> 00:12:51.437
undoing the overpolicing

00:12:51.437 --> 00:12:53.338
and oversurveilling
of black communities,

00:12:53.338 --> 00:12:55.941
and reallocating
many of the responsibilities

00:12:55.941 --> 00:12:59.011
we currently assign
to police to other safer,

00:12:59.011 --> 00:13:01.447
more effective alternatives
that don't involve someone

00:13:01.447 --> 00:13:04.016
showing up to your door
with a badge and a gun.

00:13:04.016 --> 00:13:07.253
-It's actually about
not having no police, right?

00:13:07.253 --> 00:13:10.555
But making sure, again, that
communities have the resources

00:13:10.555 --> 00:13:13.492
so that you can have less of
a footprint of police.

00:13:13.492 --> 00:13:15.060
Right?
So I'll give you an example.

00:13:15.060 --> 00:13:16.094
Lots of people have been
asking me

00:13:16.094 --> 00:13:17.563
for the last couple of days,
"Hey,

00:13:17.563 --> 00:13:20.499
if we de-fund the police, what
happens when you call 911?"

00:13:20.499 --> 00:13:22.200
And what I say back is,

00:13:22.200 --> 00:13:25.337
"Well, if something's on fire,
what number do you call?"

00:13:25.337 --> 00:13:26.605
You call 911.

00:13:26.605 --> 00:13:28.440
And who shows up?
It's the ambulance.

00:13:28.440 --> 00:13:30.042
Or, sorry, it's the firetruck.

00:13:30.042 --> 00:13:33.211
And if somebody's having
a heart attack, you call 911.

00:13:33.211 --> 00:13:34.746
And the EMT shows up.

00:13:34.746 --> 00:13:36.748
So we already have 911

00:13:36.748 --> 00:13:39.284
giving lots of different
emergency services.

00:13:39.284 --> 00:13:40.819
If the resources
that folks needed

00:13:40.819 --> 00:13:42.087
so they didn't need to rely on

00:13:42.087 --> 00:13:44.790
law enforcement
were there, all right?

00:13:44.790 --> 00:13:48.927
If 911 had more options,
communities would feel safer,

00:13:48.927 --> 00:13:51.029
and you wouldn't be introducing
a badge and a gun

00:13:51.029 --> 00:13:53.432
to situations that law
enforcement can never be trained

00:13:53.432 --> 00:13:55.901
to manage in the first place
and that they have been calling

00:13:55.901 --> 00:13:58.804
to get out of the business
of for years.

00:13:58.804 --> 00:14:01.239
That's what the majority
of protesters and activists

00:14:01.239 --> 00:14:03.576
I talk to say that they want.

00:14:03.576 --> 00:14:05.143
-Exactly.

00:14:05.143 --> 00:14:07.145
Even a former police chief in
New Orleans and Nashville said,

00:14:07.145 --> 00:14:09.248
"90% of all
the police department calls

00:14:09.248 --> 00:14:11.517
that I've looked at in my life
have nothing to do

00:14:11.517 --> 00:14:13.552
with a major Uniform Crime."

00:14:13.552 --> 00:14:15.554
Let's spend the money we're
lavishing on police departments

00:14:15.554 --> 00:14:16.989
on other nonviolent
alternatives,

00:14:16.989 --> 00:14:19.792
like mental health resources
or substance abuse resources.

00:14:19.792 --> 00:14:21.693
Or, if Tucker Carlson's
the one calling,

00:14:21.693 --> 00:14:23.595
we can send the woke militia
to force-feed him,

00:14:23.595 --> 00:14:25.530
I don't know, vegan sausage.
Maybe he'll like it.

00:14:25.530 --> 00:14:28.033
Maybe that'll be
the end of it all.

00:14:28.033 --> 00:14:30.502
Look, maybe we can just listen
to the activists

00:14:30.502 --> 00:14:32.304
and the organizers
who are doing the work

00:14:32.304 --> 00:14:34.506
instead of spending time
nitpicking their slogans.

00:14:34.506 --> 00:14:37.075
But if you're looking
for synonyms

00:14:37.075 --> 00:14:38.243
for de-funding the police,

00:14:38.243 --> 00:14:40.712
President Thesaurus has,
like, plenty of ideas.

00:14:40.712 --> 00:14:43.415
-De-funding our police,
dismantling our police,

00:14:43.415 --> 00:14:46.418
disbanding our police,
ending our police force.

00:14:46.418 --> 00:14:48.020
-This has been "A Closer Look."

00:14:48.020 --> 00:14:51.490
♪♪

00:14:51.490 --> 00:14:53.459 line:0%
As New York struggles
to reopen this week,

00:14:53.459 --> 00:14:55.627 line:0%
remember that we're still
a city in crisis,

00:14:55.627 --> 00:14:57.663 line:0%
and City Harvest has been
stepping up

00:14:57.663 --> 00:14:59.164 line:0%
to meet the increased need.

00:14:59.164 --> 00:15:01.032 line:0%
If you're watching this online,
you can hit the "donate" button.

00:15:01.032 --> 00:15:03.869 line:0%
Stay safe. Wash your hands.
We love you.

